WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.090
The word yoga comes from a
Sanskrit root meaning to yoke,

2
00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:05.560
or to join.

3
00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.680
Most people think of postures.

4
00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:13.400
But Hindu texts call yoga a path to
liberation from the cycle of rebirth.

5
00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.260
Now picture three people.

6
00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:17.150
One loves to think.

7
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.880
One loves to work.

8
00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:21.700
One loves God with all their heart.

9
00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:25.480
Can all three reach the same
goal, by different roads?

10
00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:28.490
In this mission, you'll
explore the paths of action,

11
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.510
knowledge and devotion
in the Bhagavad Gita.

12
00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:36.670
Then you'll read Krishna's words on doing
your duty without craving its results.

13
00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.380
Your mission: find out
whether the thinker,

14
00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.000
the worker and the lover of
God can reach the same goal.
